field.div:
Dear ${candidate_name},
We are delighted to offer you the role of ${job_title} in ${department} at ${company}, based at ${location}, starting on ${start_date}.
What you would be paid: ${lines}
That is ${monthly_total} a month and ${annual_total} over a year.
You would report to ${manager}. This offer is made on the understanding that the documents we have asked you for are in order and that your references confirm what you have told us.
If you are happy to accept, say so on the page in the email that brought you this letter, then sign a copy and send it back to your recruiter. If anything here is not what you expected, tell us — we would far rather talk about it than lose you over it.
We hope you will join us.
${company}
${date}

Dear ${candidate_name},
Following our conversations, ${company} is pleased to offer you the position of ${job_title} in ${department}, based at ${location}, with a proposed start date of ${start_date}.
Your pay would be made up as follows: ${lines}
In total that is ${monthly_total} a month, or ${annual_total} over a full year, in ${currency}.
You would report to ${manager}. Your employment would be on a labour contract signed on or before your first day, and the statutory insurances and personal income tax are handled by ${company} in the usual way. A probation period applies as set out in that contract.
This offer depends on the documents we have asked you for reaching us, and on your references.
To accept, use the page in the email that brought you this letter, then sign a copy and return it to your recruiter. If anything here is not what you were expecting, please tell us.
We very much hope you will join us.
${company}
${date}
